0..75 Comment "// Self-reference dissolves into the reified stack: a suspended computation"
76..153 Comment "// reaches its locals in the window its frame holds, never by an address into"
154..230 Comment "// itself, so a view lent before a suspension reads its cell after the stack"
231..305 Comment "// resumes. Rust pins a future whose state borrows from itself (`Pin`, RFC"
306..364 Comment "// 2349); C++ keeps such an object immobile by convention."
366..442 Comment "/// A view read after a suspension: the stack holding the access is resumed,"
443..495 Comment "/// and the view reads the cell it was lent (#1183)."
